ose chokepoint is a constructed-instance method (`pkg.NewX().Method(args)` style) where the constructor is cheap and takes no ports: build a fresh chokepoint per iteration via the documented constructor; the burst's value is the assertion that the package's method-internal pure logic has no package-level shared state AND that the documented constructor stays cheap and reusable. (2) `THE VALUE-FREE PROJECTION CANARY SEEDS THE SECRET MARKER INTO EVERY LEVEL OF THE VARIABLE HIERARCHY (org/project/env/service) AND ASSERTS MARKER-ABSENCE IN THREE REDACTED SURFACES: Summary JSON, slog LogValue group, AND Summary.String() form`. Unlike BE-0406's single-surface canary (ProposedDisplay survival + closed-set-tag absence), the renderer's redaction contract spans three concrete projection surfaces — the JSON-marshalled Summary, the slog handler's text output, and the single-line String form — because each is a separate code path the redactor must enforce. Forward-applicable to every verification story whose chokepoint emits a type that implements slog.LogValuer alongside an explicit Summary projection: drive the marker-absence canary through ALL THREE projection surfaces (encoding/json output, slog.NewTextHandler captured output, and any documented String form), not just the JSON; a regression in any one surface ships to a different operator audience (audit pipeline vs structured log handler vs ad-hoc fmt.Println) and pinning all three end-to-end keeps the redaction contract bound to the public API, not just the wire format. One renderer-canonical gotcha worth pinning forward: `domain.ID FIXTURES IN THE dokploy_test PACKAGE MUST USE A 26-CHAR CROCKFORD-BASE32-LOWERCASE SUFFIX EXCLUDING i, l, o, u; the canonical pair uses serviceDesiredStateFixedID(domain.KindXxx, last byte ∈ {a, b, c, d}) — last bytes from the safe set keep determinism self-check #6's reflect.DeepEqual stable across runs without invented IDs that LOOK 26-char-valid but carry excluded letters. The canonical pair file lives in `package dokploy_test` (mirrors BE-0406's `package migrateimport_test`) — the chokepoint is exported (Render is a public method on Renderer) so the canonical pair stays in the _test package next to renderer_test.go rather than the package-internal store_test convention used by the BE-0404 break-glass pair. Load-bearing invariant unchanged: ONE FILE, SIX SURFACES, SELF-CHECK; drift on any surface fails ONE test, not six.
