ralph/progress.txt:29981:  - `internal/controlplane/migrateimport/import_dry_run_canonical_test.go` — canonical pair `TestImportDryRunCoversCallSites` + `TestImportDryRunPreservesContractUnderContention` for the port-driven-pure-classifier chokepoint `(*migrateimport.Importer).Plan(ctx, PlanInput) (Plan, error)`. Walks a closed scenario table covering all 6 `ItemStatus` values (`ready`, `pending_owner`, `skip_duplicate`, `skip_missing_parent`, `skip_unsupported_type`, `skip_already_imported`) and all 6 `ItemReason` values. Four head-of-test self-checks: status exhaustiveness, reason exhaustiveness, deterministic ordering on every scenario, marker non-emptiness. Per-row redaction canary seeds `importsecretmarker` into Dokploy display names and asserts marker survival in `ProposedDisplay` plus marker absence in `string(Level)`/`string(Status)`/`string(Reason)` of every emitted item. Per-row dry-run purity canary scans `fakeRepo.calls` for any `CreateProject:`/`CreateEnvironment:`/`CreateService:` prefix; pending-owner row additionally asserts `len(repo.calls) == 0` (no-owner short-circuit). Burst is 32 × 64 = 2048 iterations; each goroutine builds its own (Snapshot, fake Repository, Importer) triple so the contention asserts the planner's internal pure helpers (`classify`, `pendingOwnerItems`, `proposeSlug`, `indexProjectsByID`, `indexEnvironmentsByID`, `indexServicesByID`) have no package-level shared state.
ralph/progress.txt:30009:    - The chokepoint is `(*Importer).Plan(ctx, in)` not a package-level pure function — so the burst can't share a single chokepoint instance the way BE-0405's reconcile burst does. Each goroutine builds its own Importer via `migrateimport.New(Config{Scanner, Repository, Logger: io.Discard})`; the burst's value shifts from "package has no shared state" to "the planner's internal pure helpers have no package-level shared state".
ralph/progress.txt:30130:  - The canonical pair for a public-method chokepoint (Render is a public method on *Renderer) lives in `package dokploy_test`, not `package dokploy` — mirroring BE-0406's `package migrateimport_test` convention for `Importer.Plan`. The BE-0404 break-glass pair lives in `package store` (not `package store_test`) only because the validator there is package-internal. The rule is: canonical pair package matches the chokepoint's visibility — public method → `pkg_test`, internal helper → `pkg`.
ralph/progress.txt:33802:  - The provisioner `DokployClient` interface now includes `EnsureService`; future compose/database service jobs can reuse the same client method but must select the correct service type and persisted Dokploy resource kind.
