+## 2026-05-18 20:45 +03 - BE-0502
+- What was implemented: Added durable worker execution for `import_dokploy_resource`, including typed organization-scoped payload validation, desired-version and cross-tenant refusal before scanning, `migrateimport.Importer` integration, and a store-backed import repository that writes each imported source-of-truth row plus its `dokploy_refs` mapping atomically.
+- Files changed: `internal/controlplane/worker/import_dokploy_resource.go`, `internal/controlplane/worker/provisioner.go`, `internal/controlplane/worker/provisioner_test.go`, `internal/controlplane/worker/AGENTS.md`, `ralph/prd.json`, `ralph/progress.txt`.
+- Verification run: `gofmt -w .`; `go mod tidy`; `go test ./internal/controlplane/worker -run 'TestImportDokployResourcePayloadValidation|TestProvisionerImportDokployResource'`; `go test ./internal/controlplane/migrateimport ./internal/controlplane/worker`; `go test ./internal/controlplane/...`; `go test ./...`; `go test -race ./...`; `go vet ./...`; `go test -run TestMigrations ./...`; `go test -run TestFakeDokploy ./...`; `go test -run TestImport ./internal/controlplane/...`; `golangci-lint run ./...`.
+- Results: All runnable checks passed. `goimports`, `staticcheck`, and `govulncheck` are not installed in this environment. Postgres-backed tests use the shared harness and skip when `YALLA_TEST_DATABASE_URL` is unset.
+- Remaining risks or follow-ups: A production Dokploy scanner adapter is still supplied through `ProvisionerConfig.ImportScanner`; this story wires the durable worker boundary and store-backed importer apply path, not the later admin API wiring.
+- **Learnings for future iterations:**
+  - `migrateimport.Importer` can be reused directly by workers as long as the concrete repository adapter keeps tenant scope from the job organization and inserts Yalla rows plus `dokploy_refs` in one transaction.
+  - Import replays should rely on existing ref classification (`skip_already_imported`) instead of special replay flags; that keeps partial-success retries deterministic.
+  - `provisioning_jobs.payload` is still `map[string]string`, so import jobs carry only stable non-secret identifiers and the worker reconstructs the richer `OwnerAssignment` internally.
+---

